Thank you so much for your help. I tried to use your advices but again the model doesn’t run. I’m really not able to get where is the mistake. I hope you’re available to supervise my script.

After opening the following libraries

library(sem)

library(lavaan)

library(semPlot)

library(foreign)

I open my dataset with this function

MYDATA <- read.spss(file.choose(),to.data.frame=TRUE)

summary(MYDATA)

Then I give <- command to create the variables

#Enacted stigma

EDS <- 'C1_1 + C1_2 + C1_3 + C1_4 + C1_5 + C1_6 + C1_7 + C1_8 + C1_9'

GSD.GENERAL <- 'C2_1 + C2_2 + C2_3 + C2_4 + C2_5'

GSD.VERBAL.ABUSES <- 'C2_7 + C2_8 + C2_9'

GSD.PHYSICAL.ABUSES <- 'C20 + C21 + C22'

GSD.SEXUAL.ABUSES <- 'C23 + C24 + C25'

#Internalized homophobia

PRIDE <- 'D2_1_r + D2_3_r + D2_7_r + D2_9_r + D2_11_r + D2_12_r + D2_14_r'

SHAME <- 'D2_4 + D2_27 + D20 + D26 + D2_29 + D29 + D2_30 + D2_32'

PASSING <- 'D2_6 + D2_31 + D2_28 + D25 + D2_23 + D23 + D2_21'

ALIENATION <- 'D2_37 + D2_38 + D2_39'

# Negative mental health outcomes

BAI <- 'F1_1 + F1_2 + F1_3 + F1_4+ F1_5 + F1_6 + F1_7 + F1_8 + F1_9+ F1_10 + F1_11 + F1_12 + F1_13 + F1_14 + F1_15 + F1_16+ F1_17 + F1_18 + F1_19 + F1_20 + F1_21'

CESD <- 'F2_1 + F2_2 + F2_3 + F2_4_r + F2_5 + F2_6 + F2_7 + F2_8_r + F2_9 + F2_10 + F2_11 + F2_12_r + F2_13 + F2_14_1 + F2_15 + F2_16_r + F2_17 + F2_18 + F2_19 + F2_20’

Then, I create my X, Y and M variable as follows

# Creation of X, Y e M

X <- 'EDS + GSD_GENERAL + GSD.VERBAL.ABUSES + GSD.PHYSICAL.ABUSES + GSD.SEXUAL.ABUSES'

M <- 'PRIDE + SHAME + PASSING + ALIENATION'

Y <- 'BAI + CESD'

And then I create the mediation model (Model 1)

#Path Model

Model1 <-'Y ~ c*X

M ~ a*X

Y ~ b*M

ab := a*b

total := c + (a*b)

’

fit1 <- sem(Model1, data = MYDATA)

summary(fit1, fit.measures = TRUE)

For the model with latent variables, I tried to create it in the following way:

Model2 <- 'X2 =~ EDS + GSD_GENERAL + GSD_VERBAL_ABUSES + GSD_PHYSICAL_ABUSES + GSD_SEXUAL_ABUSES

M2 =~ PRIDE + SHAME + PASSING + ALIENATION

Y2 =~ BAI + CESD

Y2 ~ c*X2

M2 ~ a*X2

Y2 ~ b*M2

ab := a*b

total := c + (a*b)

'

fit2 <- sem(Model2, data=MYDATA)

summary(fit2, fit.measures=TRUE)

Are you able to get where I’m wrong? I’m so sorry for this. Maybe for most people who know R it is the base, but really I’m very new.

Thanks so much again.

